BT
/F1 18 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 770 Tm (The Power Within: What Charles Haanel's Foreword Reveals About Changing Your Life) Tj
/F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 736 Tm (The forgotten inner force that can transform the way you think, act and live) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 717 Tm (What if the greatest difference between success and failure is not your circumstances,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 702 Tm (your background or your physical ability? What if it begins with the way you think? In) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 687 Tm (the foreword to *The Master Key System*, Charles Francis Haanel presents a powerful idea:) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 672 Tm (the mind is the creative force behind human progress. Some people appear to move towards) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 657 Tm (success with confidence and clarity. Others struggle for years to achieve the same) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 642 Tm (ambitions. Some give up before they begin. Haanel asks us to consider why this happens.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 627 Tm (His answer is that the most important difference is mental.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 604 Tm (The power that already exists within you) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 585 Tm (Haanel's foreword suggests that people often look outside themselves for the source of) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 570 Tm (their strength. They may wait for the right person, the right opportunity, better) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 555 Tm (circumstances or external approval before taking action. But his central message is that) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 540 Tm (power comes from within. When a person begins to recognise their own ability to think,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 525 Tm (choose and act deliberately, something important changes. They stop seeing themselves as) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 510 Tm (completely dependent on outside conditions. They begin to take responsibility for the) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 495 Tm (direction of their thoughts, their actions and their life. This does not mean that) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 480 Tm (external circumstances are irrelevant. Life contains genuine difficulties and challenges.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 465 Tm (It means that our inner response to those circumstances can influence the decisions we) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 450 Tm (make and the possibilities we are able to see.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 427 Tm (Why thought must be applied) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 408 Tm (Haanel does not present thought as a vague form of positive thinking. The foreword) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 393 Tm (repeatedly connects mental power with: Proper application. Diligence. Concentration.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 378 Tm (Understanding. Practice. Definite principles. This is important. Simply reading about) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 363 Tm (personal development is not the same as developing yourself. A person can read dozens of) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 348 Tm (books, listen to countless lectures and collect endless information without creating) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 333 Tm (meaningful change. Knowledge begins to become powerful when it is applied. The real) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 318 Tm (question is not only: **What do I know?** The deeper question is: **What am I practising) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 303 Tm (consistently?**) Tj
/F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 280 Tm (Your thoughts can create direction-or confusion) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 261 Tm (The foreword explains that the mind can contribute to favourable conditions, but it can) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 246 Tm (also reinforce negative conditions. When people repeatedly imagine lack, limitation, fear) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 231 Tm (and discord, these thoughts can influence the way they see their lives and respond to) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 216 Tm (their circumstances. This does not mean that a person is responsible for every difficult) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 201 Tm (event that happens to them. It means that repeated patterns of thought can affect: What) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 186 Tm (they notice. What they believe is possible. How they interpret setbacks. Which) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 171 Tm (opportunities they recognise. How confidently they take action. The people and) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 156 Tm (environments they move towards. A person who constantly expects failure may ignore) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 141 Tm (opportunities that are directly in front of them. A person who begins developing courage,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 126 Tm (clarity and concentration may start noticing possibilities that were previously hidden by) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 111 Tm (fear or confusion.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 34 Tm (Unleash Your Power with Tariq - 1 / 4) Tj
