/F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 770 Tm (The law of cause and effect) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 751 Tm (One of the main themes in Haanel's foreword is the relationship between cause and effect.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 736 Tm (The scientific method seeks to understand why things happen. When a desired result is) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 721 Tm (identified, the next step is to discover the conditions that produce it. Haanel applies) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 706 Tm (this idea to personal development. If someone wants greater concentration, they need to) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 691 Tm (practise concentration. If someone wants more clarity, they need to examine their) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 676 Tm (thinking and reduce mental confusion. If someone wants to become more disciplined, they) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 661 Tm (need to develop a daily practice that requires discipline. A result does not appear) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 646 Tm (simply because it is desired. It develops through the repeated conditions that support) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 631 Tm (it.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 608 Tm (The importance of concentration) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 589 Tm (Concentration is one of the most important ideas in the foreword. Without concentration,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 574 Tm (thought becomes scattered. A person may want success, health, confidence, peace and) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 559 Tm (financial security, but if their attention moves constantly from one fear to another,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 544 Tm (their mental energy becomes divided. Concentration means learning to direct attention) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 529 Tm (towards one chosen idea or purpose. This requires practice. You may sit quietly and) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 514 Tm (discover that your mind moves constantly. You may attempt to focus and find yourself) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 499 Tm (thinking about yesterday, tomorrow, unfinished tasks or imagined problems. This does not) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 484 Tm (mean you have failed. It means you have discovered the condition of your attention. Each) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 469 Tm (time you notice that your mind has wandered and calmly return it to your chosen subject,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 454 Tm (you are practising concentration.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 431 Tm (The Master Key is not a promise of something for nothing) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 412 Tm (The foreword makes an important distinction. It presents *The Master Key System* as a) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 397 Tm (study of mental principles, not as magic or a shortcut to instant results. The message is) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 382 Tm (not that something can be gained without effort. Instead, the student is encouraged to) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 367 Tm (understand the principles and apply them consistently. This is what makes the system) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 352 Tm (practical. It asks the student to: Study an idea. Understand its meaning. Practise it) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 337 Tm (repeatedly. Observe the results. Refine their application. Continue with greater) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 322 Tm (awareness. The value is found in the application.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 299 Tm (Developing the qualities within you) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 280 Tm (According to the foreword, the study of mental principles can help develop qualities such) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 265 Tm (as: Greater energy. Discernment. Mental flexibility. Stronger reasoning. Better memory.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 250 Tm (Initiative. Persistence. Wisdom in decision-making. Imagination. Definite desire.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 235 Tm (Intelligent sympathy. A greater appreciation of life. These qualities are not developed) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 220 Tm (by wishing for them. They develop through repeated thought and action. A person becomes) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 205 Tm (more courageous by repeatedly choosing courage. A person becomes more disciplined by) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 190 Tm (repeatedly acting with discipline. A person becomes more focused by repeatedly returning) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 175 Tm (their attention to what matters.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 34 Tm (Unleash Your Power with Tariq - 2 / 4) Tj
ET
