/F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 770 Tm (From fear and limitation to courage and possibility) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 751 Tm (One of the most powerful passages in the foreword describes replacing thoughts of) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 736 Tm (failure, despair, lack, limitation and discord with thoughts of courage, power,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 721 Tm (inspiration and harmony. This should not be misunderstood as pretending that problems do) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 706 Tm (not exist. The practice is not to deny difficulty. It is to stop allowing difficulty to) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 691 Tm (become the only thing you can see. When a person repeatedly gives attention to fear, fear) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 676 Tm (can dominate their decisions. When a person begins giving attention to courage, purpose) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 661 Tm (and constructive action, their choices can begin to change. They may become more willing) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 646 Tm (to communicate, learn, take responsibility, ask for help, pursue an opportunity or begin) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 631 Tm (again after a setback. This is how inner change can begin influencing outer behaviour.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 608 Tm (Questions are searchlights) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 589 Tm (The foreword describes questions as powerful tools in the search for understanding. This) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 574 Tm (is a useful idea for anyone beginning a personal-development journey. Good questions) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 559 Tm (direct attention. Instead of asking: **Why does everything always go wrong for me?** You) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 544 Tm (might ask: **What can I learn from this situation?** Instead of asking: **Why am I unable) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 529 Tm (to change?** You might ask: **What small action can I repeat today?** Instead of asking:) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 514 Tm (**What is missing from my life?** You might ask: **What ability do I need to develop) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 499 Tm (next?** The quality of your questions can influence the direction of your thinking.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 476 Tm (A new way to approach personal development) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 457 Tm (The foreword describes the possibility of a new consciousness and a new understanding of) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 442 Tm (the resources within the self. In practical terms, this means becoming more aware of your) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 427 Tm (inner life. You begin observing: The thoughts you repeat. The emotions you strengthen.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 412 Tm (The images you hold in your mind. The purpose you return to. The actions you take each) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 397 Tm (day. The conditions that support or weaken your progress. This approach makes personal) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 382 Tm (development active. You are no longer simply waiting to feel motivated. You are creating) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 367 Tm (a structure that helps you practise the qualities you want to develop.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 344 Tm (Your daily practice begins with one thought) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 325 Tm (You do not need to transform your entire life in one day. Begin with one thought. Choose) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 310 Tm (one constructive quality you want to develop, such as: Calmness. Courage. Concentration.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 295 Tm (Patience. Confidence. Discipline. Clarity. Purpose. Sit quietly for a few minutes and) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 280 Tm (bring your attention back to that quality whenever your mind wanders. Then ask yourself:) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 265 Tm (**How can I express this quality in one practical action today?** This is how thought) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 250 Tm (begins to become application.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 34 Tm (Unleash Your Power with Tariq - 3 / 4) Tj
